{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every simple path of a directed graph from a source to any of a set of targets, lazily, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order a depth-first search from the source, taking out-edges in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" order, reaches them."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/ST"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"DirectedSimplePaths","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/SimplePaths.swift#L222","fileName":"SimplePaths.swift"},"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedSimplePaths"}],"externalID":"s:9Traversal19DirectedSimplePathsV","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Traversal"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedSimplePaths"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","text":"DirectedGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each copy of a parallel edge gives a different path. A path reaching one target continues to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the others, so a path through a target to another is listed after the shorter one. The source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"itself, when it is a target, gives the trivial path first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sequence holds the graph (a value), so iterating again gives the same paths. The first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"text":" copies the rows the source reaches, O(n + m). A vertex that reaches no target is never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entered, but a partial path can still end where every way on is blocked by its own vertices,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the time between two paths is not bounded by a polynomial in n + m.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traversal\/directedsimplepaths"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Iterator"],"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/maxLength"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/makeIterator()"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Element"],"title":"Type Aliases","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases"},{"identifiers":["doc